{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1112266-cofd-for-dummies","id":1112266,"title":"CofD For Dummies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-06T12:19:54-07:00","id":1112266,"title":"CofD For Dummies","content":"I asked this question on RPG Net &quot;I really like Chronicles of Darkness but it's way too complex for me to run.&quot; To clarify, I super like the setting and think the mechanics are neat.<br /> <br /> Without replicating it in Fate or Apocalypse World (which is the usual suggestion for this kind of thing), what could I do, if anything, to make it more GM-able for me (at least at first, until I master all the stuff).<br /> <br /> One RPGNet poster suggested:<br /> * replace written outcomes of dramatic failure and extraordinary success with GM / player narrative outcomes (even if a condition is specified)<br /> <br /> Another thought I had, and I have no idea if this would work, is<br /> * replace subsystems w/ extended tests (e.g., social maneuvering and doors with an extended normal check) or simple tests (e.g., you just have a cover score if you're a demon and you roll that).<br /> <br /> I also own all the Mirrors and Chronicler's guides from CoD v1 so if there's anything in there I should use just tell me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?806673-Slightly-Simplified-Chronicles-of-Darkness\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...es-of-Darkness</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:21:47-07:00","id":1112268,"title":"","content":"Have a big list of names and previously-created stat blocks for NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:45:56-07:00","id":1112283,"title":"","content":"If you're going to replace the subsystems with generic rolls (which is always intended to be an option), I recommend using instant actions rather than extended.<br /> <br /> CofD &quot;telescopes&quot; pretty well. You can start out playing the game (even combat) with just basic skill checks and the occasional improvised Condition until you feel a need for the more complex rules (if ever). Even most supernatural powers can just be dealt with in terms of what they logically do, rather than in terms of how they interact with particular numbers or states.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:54:16-07:00","id":1112288,"title":"","content":"Yeah - here's the trick. Down and Dirty combat is just treating combat like any other instant action. All the social maneuvering system does is mechanise the dice pool modifiers for an instant action.<br /> <br /> If you are ever unsure, or don't want to belabour something for reasons of flow, just call for Attribute + Skill and eyeball a pool penalty or bonus that seems right. Everything else is chroming the game engine's wheelrims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:29:15-07:00","id":1112733,"title":"","content":"The CoD Core and Hunter Supplement have great rules for building antagonists with simplified stat blocks and powers. How would I adjust these guys to work as NPC/antagonists with the major splats (e.g., the Werewolf as designed for Hunter wouldn't be a credible antagonist for actual Werewolves).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:25:07-07:00","id":1112955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1112266-cofd-for-dummies?p=1112288#post1112288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah - here's the trick. Down and Dirty combat is just treating combat like any other instant action. All the social maneuvering system does is mechanise the dice pool modifiers for an instant action.<br /> <br /> If you are ever unsure, or don't want to belabour something for reasons of flow, just call for Attribute + Skill and eyeball a pool penalty or bonus that seems right. Everything else is chroming the game engine's wheelrims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Game developers need provide their avid readers with sweet mechanics sometimes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:05:22-07:00","id":1124345,"title":"","content":"For some of the game lines (VtR, WtF, MtA) antagonists / NPCs will often be other people from the same splat. HOWEVER building an NPC/Antagonist is non-trivial, and statting up a simplified NPC using Dread Powers won't quite capture things correctly.<br /> <br /> This thread (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/42870-simplified-antagonist-stat-block\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ist-stat-block</a>) talks about how people have created / approached simplified NPC-from-same-splat generation for VtM. Has anyone created something similar for CoD? Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:23:45-07:00","id":1124357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1112266-cofd-for-dummies?p=1124345#post1124345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/42870-simplified-antagonist-stat-block\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ist-stat-block</a>) talks about how people have created / approached simplified NPC-from-same-splat generation for VtM. Has anyone created something similar for CoD? Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It's in the middle of the Chronicles of Darkness book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:05:29-07:00","id":1124384,"title":"","content":"Sweet, thanks! You mean the new core book, right nofather?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:12:59-07:00","id":1124389,"title":"","content":"Yes, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/168428/Chronicles-of-Darkness\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a>. There's a section on Horrors and Wonders. If you feel Dread Powers don't fully encapsulate the abilities you want them to, you're free to use Disciplines, Gifts, Rotes, or natural abilities like Shapeshifting and Frenzy and so forth as Dread Powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:15:24-07:00","id":1124393,"title":"","content":"Neato. I saw that. They still have individual values for stats. I could probably just do Physical, Social, and Mental, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:23:06-07:00","id":1124400,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T12:48:18-07:00","id":1124441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1112266-cofd-for-dummies?p=1124393#post1124393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neato. I saw that. They still have individual values for stats. I could probably just do Physical, Social, and Mental, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how basic you want them, you could just go Brief Nightmares, and give them Best At, Worst At, and Other pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:00:07-07:00","id":1124488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1112266-cofd-for-dummies?p=1124441#post1124441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depending on how basic you want them, you could just go Brief Nightmares, and give them Best At, Worst At, and Other pools.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is how I do most antagonists or other NPCs that become antagonists suddenly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:09:54-07:00","id":1124519,"title":"","content":"I like that. does that work for person vs the same splat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:10:53-07:00","id":1124573,"title":"","content":"As an aside but somewhat related to the topic there actually is a Vampire the Requiem for Dummies. It's better for getting the basics of Vampire than really offering tips, though. The storytelling section offered some basic tips, like the Ten Best Foes of Vampires, but didn't really get into the meat of storytelling, unfortunately. I guess that's the point, it is mostly for beginners, I picked mine up when I first started the game a few months after it came out. As far as I know there were no further versions for White Wolf or Onyx Path games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T20:47:10-07:00","id":1124603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1112266-cofd-for-dummies?p=1124519#post1124519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that. does that work for person vs the same splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I use it for pretty much any character I didn't plan more detailed stats for. It's really easy to improvise. You don't even have to decide exactly what tasks an NPC is best and worst at. Just take a second whenever you need to roll a dice pool for the NPC to ask yourself &quot;Is this something this NPC should be an expert at? Is it something this NPC should struggle with?&quot; and pick based on your answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}